{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moses told.</b> Although the verse says ״וַיִּשְׁמַע״ etc. ״אֵת כָּל אֲשֶׁר״ etc., perhaps there were details that his ear had not heard. Or it may be that he did not fully validate the wonders because of the extraordinary nature of the events, or that although he had some prior knowledge of them, he still doubted whether the Egyptian yoke upon their necks had truly been broken, and Moses told him something that he could not have known on his own — namely, the slaying of the Egyptian prince, which our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Zohar 2:52b) that Israel saw him dead. And through this Jethro established as fact that their yoke had been broken from upon them." "Or perhaps this is what the verse alluded to by saying <b>et all the hardship that found you on the way and He delivered you</b> etc. — that he informed him of the pursuit of the prince, for Jethro was priest of Midian, and in any case they discern and know that there are supernal princes over every nation, and he told him that this prince pursued them in person, as it is written (Exodus 14:10): ״וְהִנֵּה מִצְרַיִם נֹסֵעַ אַחֲרֵיהֶם״ — and because of this Israel trembled and were terrified, as we explained there. And when Jethro heard this, he said <b>Blessed</b> etc. <b>from under the hand of Mitzrayim</b> — this being the prince whose name is Mitzrayim. And this is correct."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:32.609226104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}